CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*ahd->platform_data)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct ahd_platform_data)...)
#42: FILE: drivers/scsi/aic7xxx/aic79xx_osm.c:1327:
+	ahd->platform_data = kzalloc(sizeof(struct ahd_platform_data),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

